  "summary_en": "Japan's Road Act Enforcement Regulations (1952, as amended to April 2026) set procedures for road designation, ledgers, occupancy permits, maintenance standards and inspection. Only marginal autonomous-driving content: standards for 'automated operation assistance facilities' (road-side aids for self-driving vehicles) and designation of groups promoting automated driving.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Art. 4-8-2 sets performance standards for automated-operation assistance facilities (roadside aids that correct position and supply road information to self-driving vehicles).",
   "Art. 4-8-3 requires public notice of installation of such facilities.",
   "Art. 4-4-11 allows designation of associations using automated driving for sustainable transport and logistics.",
   "Art. 4-5-6 sets road/tunnel/bridge maintenance and inspection standards (close visual inspection every five years).",
   "Defines specified vehicle types and road occupancy permit procedures."
  ],
